0..64 Comment "// A complete binary tree built two ways agrees at depth twelve."
65..67 Comment "//"
68..143 Comment "// One definition builds each level once and holds it in both halves of the"
144..224 Comment "// next, so its run shares every subtree. The other builds every copy afresh, so"
225..301 Comment "// its run holds the whole tree. The two results are one tree, shared in two"
302..320 Comment "// different ways."
321..323 Comment "//"
324..403 Comment "// The conversion runs both endpoints within the tier\'s fuel. It compares their"
404..480 Comment "// readings, about 25,000 nodes, as the graphs they are shared as. A wrapper"
481..539 Comment "// over each half triples the nodes that each call builds."
540..542 Comment "//"
543..607 Comment "// - see: #3604 — the sharing-equality check this row measures"
609..630 Comment "// The free naturals."
